# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: 'Registrar: reserve and register paras from a system parachain'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |-
      Fills in the two registrar pallets and their shared wire types, so a system parachain can
      hand out para ids, hold the deposits, and drive registration on the relay chain over XCM.
      Deposits only ever live on the parachain; the relay chain takes nothing.

      Pushing a multi-megabyte validation code through an XCM `Transact` would be wasteful, so
      registration is split in two and only the code hash and length cross the bridge:

      1. `pallet-registrar-para::reserve` allocates the next free para id and holds `ParaDeposit`.
      2. `pallet-registrar-para::register` holds a deposit for the head data and the declared code
         length, and asks the relay chain to accept the registration.
      3. `pallet-registrar-relay::authorize_code` validates the request against the relay chain's
         live configuration and parks it. Only callable by a trusted XCM origin (e.g. the Coretime
         chain). A request it will not act on is rejected and reported rather than failed, so the
         parachain never sits on a stuck deposit.
      4. `pallet-registrar-relay::apply_authorized_code` takes the blob itself. It is unsigned,
         pays no fee and authorizes itself through `#[pallet::authorize]`: the pending entry
         already pins down the exact bytes that will be accepted and the manager has already paid
         for them, so anybody may submit it. A matching blob onboards the para and reports the
         outcome back.
      5. `pallet-registrar-para::receive` applies the verdict, keeping the deposit held or
         releasing it.

      Nothing on the relay chain times an authorization out: no per-block sweep runs there, and
      missing the deadline is the manager's problem rather than every block's. If the code never
      arrives, `pallet-registrar-para::cancel_registration` ends the registration and the manager
      pays for the round trip. It does not release the deposit on its own either: the relay chain
      is asked to drop the authorization and only its answer frees the funds, which is what stops a
      cancellation from refunding a para that did get registered while its verdict was lost.

      `registrar-primitives` carries the versioned wire types and depends on neither FRAME nor XCM,
      so one version of the format serves Westend, Kusama and Polkadot and neither pallet has to
      depend on the other. The `SendToRelay`/`SendToPara` traits keep XCM out of both pallets: what
      a message means is the pallet's business, how it travels is the runtime's.

      `paras_registrar` gains `do_register_without_deposit` and an implementation of the relay
      pallet's `ParachainRegistrar` trait. Head data and code are still validated against the live
      configuration and the para still goes through the usual onboarding and PVF pre-check; only
      the deposit is skipped.

      Neither pallet is wired into a production runtime yet.

crates:
  - name: registrar-primitives
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-para
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-registrar-relay
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-runtime-common
    bump: minor
